From 3f2e1a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sie-mcp web <web@sie-mcp.local>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: skip cpu_io_recompile() - MMIO poll longjmp storm

Every MMIO access from a TB whose instruction is not the TB's last
(!can_do_io, qemu 11's strict io placement for icount) triggers
cpu_io_recompile(): a cpu_loop_exit() longjmp plus re-translation of a
1-insn CF_MEMI_ONLY TB.  The original TB stays cached, so an MMIO
polling loop pays this on EVERY iteration, forever.  Natively that is a
~1us setjmp hop; under emscripten longjmp is JS-exception based and
costs ~150us of unwinding.

Measured on the S75 firmware (post-crash idle): 16,324 recompiles in
~20s across only 229 distinct TBs; 50.7% of the vCPU worker's self
time was inside __emscripten_throw_longjmp (caller stack:
cpu_io_recompile <- do_ld_mmio_beN <- do_ld4_mmu <- tci_qemu_ld).
Disabling the recompile took the sustained rate from 175k to 790k
insns/s (4.5x).

The per-instruction icount precision the recompile protects does not
exist on emscripten anyway: this tree batches icount2 accounting once
per TB in cpu_tb_exec() before execution (web patch 0002), so device
callbacks already see the end-of-TB clock.  Skipping io_prepare's
recompile changes nothing about clock visibility.
---
 accel/tcg/cputlb.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cputlb.c b/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
index 28c864839e..50914a9aa3 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
@@ -1280,9 +1280,26 @@ io_prepare(hwaddr *out_offset, CPUState *cpu, CPUTLBEntryFull *full,
     section = full->section;
     mr_offset = full->xlat_offset + addr;
     cpu->mem_io_pc = retaddr;
+#ifndef __EMSCRIPTEN__
     if (!cpu->neg.can_do_io) {
         cpu_io_recompile(cpu, retaddr);
     }
+#else
+    /*
+     * wasm: cpu_io_recompile() longjmps out of the interpreter, and
+     * emscripten's JS-based longjmp costs ~150us of unwinding.  MMIO
+     * polling loops (this machine's firmware polls constantly) would
+     * pay it on every iteration: measured 16k recompiles / 20s across
+     * only 229 TBs, 50% of the vCPU thread in __emscripten_throw_longjmp.
+     *
+     * The recompile exists so icount accounts an MMIO access with
+     * per-instruction precision (device callbacks must not see the
+     * clock of insns that have not executed yet).  On emscripten the
+     * icount2 accounting is already batched once per TB before
+     * execution (accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c), so skipping this changes
+     * nothing about clock visibility - it only stops the storm.
+     */
+#endif
 
     *out_offset = mr_offset;
     return section;
